From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pypi/build.sh: install setuptools and setuptools_scm

pypi/setup.py imports `setuptools` and `distutils.extension` and lists
`setuptools_scm` in `setup_requires`, but build.sh only installs `cython` and
`wheel` before running `setup.py sdist bdist_wheel`. That relied on the
interpreter shipping setuptools preinstalled, which manylinux images no longer
do from Python 3.12 on (the stdlib also dropped `distutils` in 3.12, which only
setuptools' shim provides back). On cp312/cp313/cp314 the build aborts with
`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'setuptools'`.

Install setuptools alongside cython and wheel, as upstream's own
pyboolector-3.2.4.19342042739 sdist on PyPI does in its build.sh (a change
never committed to the git repository). Also install setuptools_scm so the
`setup_requires` entry is already satisfied instead of going through
setuptools' deprecated `fetch_build_eggs`.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [matches upstream's own 3.2.4.19342042739 PyPI sdist, never committed to git]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/pypi/build.sh b/pypi/build.sh
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pypi/build.sh
+++ b/pypi/build.sh
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
 for py in $PYTHON_VERSIONS; do
   python=/opt/python/${py}-${py}/bin/python
   echo "Python: ${python}"
-  ${python} -m pip install cython wheel
+  ${python} -m pip install cython wheel setuptools setuptools_scm
   cd ${BUILD_DIR}/pyboolector
   rm -rf src
   cp -r ${BUILD_DIR}/boolector/src/api/python src
